MORIZON NEXT
Copyright and Attribution Notice

1. Original MORIZON

MORIZON NEXT is based on the MORIZON forest zoning plugin distributed by
the Forestry Agency of Japan (林野庁) through the Geospatial Information
Center (geospatial.jp).

The original source package contains the following notice:

  ForestZoningPlugin
  Copyright (C) 2021 MIERUNE Inc.
  Contact stated in the original source: info@mierune.co.jp

The original MORIZON was developed through a project commissioned by the
Forestry Agency of Japan. The Japan Forest Technology Association
(日本森林技術協会) organized the zoning concept and workflow, and
MIERUNE Inc. implemented the QGIS plugin.

The file templates/sagyo_system_template_220113.xlsx is the unmodified
work-system spreadsheet template ("集材作業効率の設定220113.xlsx")
distributed in the ZoningKit data packages of the same MORIZON tool on
the official Forestry Agency distribution page. Only the file name has
been changed (to ASCII).

2. MORIZON NEXT modifications

Modifications for QGIS 3.x/4.x dual compatibility, bug fixes, new
features (such as automatic data acquisition and saving/resuming an
analysis), and the MORIZON NEXT identity are undertaken as an independent technical
initiative by:

  Copyright (C) 2026 Hideharu Masai

The modifications began on 2026-09-29, when the original MORIZON v2.1
source was imported. Each modified file carries a notice stating that it
was modified. The changes and their dates are recorded in the Git history
of the repository (https://github.com/raw-slnc/morizon_next).

MORIZON NEXT is independently maintained. It is not an official
modification or release of, nor guaranteed or supported by, the Japan
Forest Technology Association or the Forestry Agency of Japan.

